## Disclo Testing Rules

- Write the test BEFORE writing the implementation for all new features (TDD). No exceptions.
- Never use `test.skip` or `it.skip` in committed code.
- Keep unit, integration, and contract tests for critical flows.
- All new functions in `packages/core` require unit tests.
- Coverage threshold: 80% for core package, 70% for adapters.
- All new API routes require integration tests.
- Security-sensitive changes require explicit regression tests.
- Mock external APIs (GPTZero, Hive, Anthropic, Stripe) — never call real APIs in unit tests.
- E2E tests (Playwright) run in CI against the Railway staging environment.
- Follow `docs/TESTING.md` for governance thresholds.
